From 00f6831a99af299485ca682d6a450406bfec5810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:53:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Hold linux-headers with the kernel

Only linux was held, so once Arch moved past the launcher's kernel, Update > Omarchy upgraded linux-headers and the DKMS hooks removed the camera and battery modules from the running kernel, then could not rebuild them for a kernel that is not installed. Hold the headers in new images, and have catch-up add them to the IgnorePkg line that holds linux on existing disks. Revision 70 also makes the initramfs extract the module tree again, which puts back the modules an Update removed.

The camera bridge waited forever for /dev/video42 and showed as active with no camera. It now gives up after 30 seconds, and the unit stays failed.
